  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Dominican sacred drumming on palos (atabales), long log drums played with sung responsorial verses at saints' festivals, velaciones and funerary rites of religious brotherhoods (cofradías). The Cofradía del Espíritu Santo de los Congos de Villa Mella, which plays its own congo drums with the canoíta and maracas, was proclaimed a UNESCO Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity; the membrane-drum card stands in for the palos and congo drums.",
  "recipe": "classic modern palos / atabales, ritual Devotional, Afro-diasporic branch. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, maracas. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
